# Kameleoon Experiment Standards

Reference: https://docs.kameleoon.com/developer-docs/apis/activation-api-js/api-reference/api-reference

## Prefer Kameleoon APIs over custom JS

| Need | Use | Avoid |
|------|-----|-------|
| Wait for selector | `Kameleoon.API.Core.runWhenElementPresent()` | `KamMutation`, custom polling |
| Wait for condition | `Kameleoon.API.Core.runWhenConditionTrue()` | `waitUntil`, `setInterval` |
| Event listeners | `Kameleoon.API.Utils.addEventListener()` | Raw `addEventListener` when Kameleoon API exists |
| Goal tracking | `Kameleoon.API.Goals.processConversion(goalId)` | Custom tracking |

Check the official API docs before writing custom DOM observation or polling.

## Migration

During migration, do not change class names, functionality, or logic. Preserve existing behavior and only update implementation details (e.g. replace legacy utilities with Kameleoon APIs) where required.

## Structure & naming

- Config object: selectors, HTML, goal IDs/names, translations
- Multiple selectors: group in config, wait via `Promise.all` + `runWhenElementPresent`
- One-time init guards: `window.__kam{Id}Initialized` to prevent duplicate bindings
- Goal names in config must match the brief exactly

## Goal tracking pattern

```javascript
if (goalId && Kameleoon?.API?.Goals?.processConversion) {
    Kameleoon.API.Goals.processConversion(goalId);
}
```

## Existing repo utilities

`100-Inchcape/utils/kamMutation.js` and `waitUntil.js` exist but are legacy. Use Kameleoon-native APIs for new code unless no equivalent exists.
